*> Several CURRENCY SIGN clauses, each WITH PICTURE SYMBOL: every
*> symbol is a currency symbol in pictures, in either case. The word
*> after PICTURE is SYMBOL here, not a picture string.
IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
PROGRAM-ID. CURRENCIES.
ENVIRONMENT DIVISION.
CONFIGURATION SECTION.
SPECIAL-NAMES.
    CURRENCY SIGN IS "EUR " WITH PICTURE SYMBOL "U",
    CURRENCY SIGN IS " ct" WITH PICTURE SYMBOL "c",
    CURRENCY SIGN IS "$US" WITH PICTURE SYMBOL "$".
DATA DIVISION.
WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
77  EUROS               PIC U99V99.
77  CENTS               PIC c9,999.
77  DOLLARS             PIC $$9.99.
PROCEDURE DIVISION.
    DISPLAY EUROS CENTS DOLLARS
    STOP RUN.
